Going deeper without more hit points or AC points means facing
meaner monsters compared to your current survivability.  Increasing
hit points to roughly match the expected level of monsters on the
next level is definitely "a definite benefit" to me.  Yes, it's the
opposite of the protection racket.  Doesn't make it an unworking
strategy.

So what would be lingering without a definite benefit?  See the
"Welcome to level 3..." message and don't head for the down
stairs without some specific plan on why you would stay at one
level for other reasons.  I've lingered on a level with an altar to
do sacs or did a little extra wandering to go find a pet.

By the time of the mines when orcs, hobbits, dwarves, elves are
being generated regularly staying for their items can end up a
definite benefit.  Because of the mine town altar, it isn't that bad
to spend extra time on that level gathering items that have been
